# pacman ships PostTransaction hooks in /usr/share/libalpm/hooks/ that refresh
# the desktop-file MIME cache and the icon theme caches. They trigger on
# `usr/share/applications/*.desktop` and `usr/share/icons/*/` for install,
# upgrade, and remove -- exactly the paths this package installs -- so
# refreshing either cache here would be redundant work, and namcap's
# `externalhooks` rule flags it. That rule substring-matches the whole file,
# comments included, so those refresher command names must not appear here at
# all. The KDE service cache is per-user and rebuilt on demand; a root-run
# rebuild would only touch root's cache and is deliberately not invoked.
#
# This hook therefore only prints the removal contract pacman cannot carry out.

post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
AI Agent Control Center is installed at /usr/bin/ai-agent-control-center.

Per-user data is created on first run under ~/.local/share, ~/.config, and
~/.cache. `pacman -R` cannot remove per-user data or stop a running instance.
Before removing the package, run ONE of:

    ai-agent-control-center --uninstall
        stop the runtime and remove app state, KEEPING the database and any
        downloaded offline-voice models

    ai-agent-control-center --purge --confirm PURGE
        stop the runtime and irreversibly delete ALL local data

The persistent KDE screen-cast / remote-desktop permission is revoked in
KDE System Settings, not by this package.
MSG
}
